The files of this directory are a modified version of the Haskell 2010 Report,
"Haskell 2010 Language Report", edited by Simon Marlow, as its sources give it at
commit 15bff26 of https://github.com/haskell/haskell-report, the commit the
online Report of 2010-07-20 (https://www.haskell.org/onlinereport/haskell2010/)
was made from; with code carried from rhc's library of Haskell 98
(share/rhc/haskell98), itself a modified version of the Haskell 98 Report, and
code from GHC's library base, version 4.3, whose documentation the Report's
library chapters are.

They are not a definition of the language Haskell 2010, and do not claim to be
one: they are part of an implementation of it, rhc.

What was changed:

  * Only the Haskell code the Report prints is here, not the Report in its
    entirety: the Prelude (chapter 9) and the four library modules it gives
    code for, Data.Array, Data.Complex, Data.Maybe and Data.Ratio (chapters 14,
    17, 21 and 22).
  * pristine/ holds that code as printed, taken mechanically from the Report's
    sources (pristine/MANIFEST.tsv). It is kept unchanged, as the text the
    modules here are compared with.
  * The modules here of those names are that code with the changes rhc makes
    to it, its overlay, and a comment at the head of each saying so.
    overlay.tsv lists every change made to the Report's code, or to be made to
    it, each with its reason; corrections.tsv lists the corrections of the
    Report's text that rhc reads it with, the Haskell 98 Report's errata among
    them, and what was done with each.
  * The modules the Report gives no code for, the other 26 of its library
    chapters, are code written for what their chapters say, and provenance.tsv
    says where each one's comes from: rhc's library of Haskell 98, base, or
    rhc itself.

PreludeBuiltin and UnicodePrims, the modules of primitives the Report's code
names and does not define, are no files here: they are rhc's runtime,
lib/language/haskell/coreruntime.sml. PreludeRuntime and PreludeEnum, rhc's
modules of what the library builds on, are a layer this library shares with
share/rhc/haskell98 (the haskell2010 roadmap's D25), not files of this
directory.

Each file of this directory is distributed under the Haskell 2010 Report's
notice, whose code or chapter it carries, and also under the Haskell 98
Report's where it holds code carried from rhc's library of Haskell 98, and
under base's licence where it holds code from base, as provenance.tsv says.
The CC0 dedication of the rest of the Rune repository, in the LICENSE at its
top, does not apply to them.

The Haskell 2010 Report's notice, as its sources give it:

  Copyright notice.

  The authors and publisher intend this Report to belong to the entire
  Haskell community, and grant permission to copy and distribute it for any
  purpose, provided that it is reproduced in its entirety, including this
  Notice. Modified versions of this Report may also be copied and
  distributed for any purpose, provided that the modified version is clearly
  presented as such, and that it does not claim to be a definition of the
  language Haskell 2010.

